HTTP responses: Status Line and Status Codes
Every first line of http responses called Status line.
Status line consisted with HTTP version, Status code, Reason Phrase.
In status line, Status code means short three-digit numbers that showing the outcome of request
Reason Phrase is short message that explains the status code.

Common status codes : 
100 : continue(waiting additional response)
200 : OK
301 : Moved permanantly
404 : Not found
500 : Internal Server Error

Response Header
Key headers in response header : Content-type / Content=length / Date
Content-type : what kind of content it's getting. like HTML,JSON. also includes character set (like UTF-8)

Other Common Response Headers
Set-cookie : sends cookies from the server to the client.
To keep things secure, cookie must set with the HttpOnly / Secure flag.
Cache-control: tells how long it can cache the response before checking with the server again











